  "blocks": {
    "a-ticket-nobody-owns-text-4": {
      "id": "a-ticket-nobody-owns-text-4",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Zhaoyang Yu*, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Aoyang Fang*",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", Minghua Ma, Jaskaran Singh Walia, Chaoyun Zhang, Shu Chi, Ze Li, Murali Chintalapati, Xuchao Zhang, Rujia Wang, Chetan Bansal, Saravan Rajmohan, Qingwei Lin, Shenglin Zhang, Dan Pei, Pinjia He (* equal contribution). "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "ASE 2025",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", 674–686. Directly accepted; deployed in production at a leading global technology company."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://profile.aoyangfang.top/assets/publications/ase25/ASE_triangle.pdf",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PDF"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://doi.org/10.1109/ASE63991.2025.00062",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "DOI"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " · "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "href": "https://aka.ms/triangle-open-source",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Code"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An incident ticket rarely says which team owns the problem; the evidence sits in each team’s own logs. Triangle gives every team an LLM agent that reads those logs, adds what it finds to the ticket and votes on the owner. In production it cut Time to Engage by up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "91%",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". On three months of production incidents it finds the right team within five hops 91.7% of the time, against 67.6% for DeepCT."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "only": [
        "web"
      ]
    },
    "a-ticket-nobody-owns--scene": {
      "id": "a-ticket-nobody-owns--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "a-ticket-nobody-owns--scene--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "scene": "a-ticket-nobody-owns",
        "alt": "A sign-in ticket hops from Team A to B to C, each hop adding to the wait; then Figure 3 shows triage time climbing with every hop."
      }
    },
    "the-answer-isn-t-in-the-ticket-text-7": {
      "id": "the-answer-isn-t-in-the-ticket-text-7",
      "type": "text",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Incidents arrive as sparse alerts or vague complaints, and similar problems are described in different words. The knowledge that decides ownership belongs to many teams and keeps changing, so a misrouted incident hops from team to team while the system stays degraded. Across more than 3,000 teams over 12 months, median triage time and human discussion turns grow exponentially with the number of transfer hops."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The best prior method, DeepCT, learns from the discussions engineers write while they investigate, so it routes well only after people have done the work."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "only": [
        "web"
      ]
    },
    "the-answer-isn-t-in-the-ticket-image-9": {
      "id": "the-answer-isn-t-in-the-ticket-image-9",
      "type": "image",
      "assetId": "the-answer-isn-t-in-the-ticket-asset-8",
